{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Bring her out and let her be burned.</b> They accepted it from him immediately, and from this you learn that he was the judge, and such was their practice, that any woman who committed adultery was [condemned] to burning. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: Tamar was the daughter of Shem, and he was priest to El Elyon; therefore he judged her by burning, for such is the law of the Torah, as it is said (Leviticus 21:9): ״ובת איש כהן כי תחל לזנות וגו׳ באש תשרף״ — 'And the daughter of a priest, when she begins to commit harlotry… with fire she shall be burned.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:40.336210174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}